msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# AutoTune Guide\n"
"\n"
"AutoTune is a tool for automatically tuning database kernel parameters. It analyzes the current workload and system status, and automatically adjusts database parameters to achieve optimal performance.\n"
"\n"
"## Installation\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"pip install auto-tune\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Quick Start\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"from auto_tune import AutoTuner\n"
"\n"
"# Create tuner instance\n"
"tuner = AutoTuner(\n"
"    db_type=\"postgresql\",\n"
"    host=\"localhost\",\n"
"    port=5432,\n"
"    username=\"postgres\",\n"
"    password=\"your_password\"\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"# Run tuning\n"
"results = tuner.tune()\n"
"print(results)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Configuration\n"
"\n"
"### Basic Configuration\n"
"\n"
"| Parameter | Description | Default Value |\n"
"|-----------|-------------|---------------|\n"
"| `db_type` | Database type (postgresql/mysql) | None |\n"
"| `host` | Database host address | localhost |\n"
"| `port` | Database port | 5432 |\n"
"| `username` | Database username | None |\n"
"| `password` | Database password | None |\n"
"\n"
"### Advanced Configuration\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"tuner = AutoTuner(\n"
"    db_type=\"postgresql\",\n"
"    host=\"localhost\",\n"
"    port=5432,\n"
"    username=\"postgres\",\n"
"    password=\"your_password\",\n"
"    # Advanced configuration\n"
"    tuning_interval=3600,  # Tuning interval (seconds)\n"
"    max_iterations=100,    # Maximum number of tuning iterations\n"
"    target_metric=\"throughput\",  # Target optimization metric\n"
"    safe_mode=True         # Safe mode (only adjust safe parameters)\n"
")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Tuning Process\n"
"\n"
"1. **Workload Analysis**: Analyze current database workload characteristics\n"
"2. **Parameter Collection**: Collect current database parameter configurations\n"
"3. **Performance Baseline**: Establish current performance baseline\n"
"4. **Parameter Optimization**: Optimize parameters using machine learning algorithms\n"
"5. **Effect Verification**: Verify the effect of parameter adjustments\n"
"\n"
"## Supported Parameters\n"
"\n"
"### PostgreSQL\n"
"\n"
"- `shared_buffers`: Shared buffer size\n"
"- `work_mem`: Working memory size\n"
"- `maintenance_work_mem`: Maintenance working memory\n"
"- `effective_cache_size`: Effective cache size\n"
"- `wal_buffers`: WAL log buffer size\n"
"- `max_connections`: Maximum number of connections\n"
"\n"
"### MySQL\n"
"\n"
"- `innodb_buffer_pool_size`: InnoDB buffer pool size\n"
"- `innodb_log_file_size`: InnoDB log file size\n"
"- `max_connections`: Maximum number of connections\n"
"- `query_cache_size`: Query cache size\n"
"- `tmp_table_size`: Temporary table size\n"
"\n"
"## API Reference\n"
"\n"
"### AutoTuner Class\n"
"\n"
"#### `tune()`\n"
"Execute automatic tuning and return tuning results.\n"
"\n"
"**Return Value**: Dictionary containing tuning suggestions and expected performance improvements.\n"
"\n"
"#### `get_current_config()`\n"
"Get current database parameter configuration.\n"
"\n"
"**Return Value**: Dictionary of parameter names and their current values.\n"
"\n"
"#### `get_tuning_history()`\n"
"Get historical tuning records.\n"
"\n"
"**Return Value**: List of historical tuning records.\n"
"\n"
"#### `apply_config(config)`\n"
"Apply specified parameter configuration.\n"
"\n"
"**Parameters**:\n"
"- `config`: Dictionary of parameter names and values to be applied\n"
"\n"
"#### `reset_config()`\n"
"Reset all parameters to database default values.\n"
"\n"
"## Command Line Tool\n"
"\n"
"AutoTune also provides a command line tool:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"# Basic usage\n"
"auto-tune --db-type postgresql --host localhost --port 5432\n"
"\n"
"# Specify username and password\n"
"auto-tune --db-type mysql --username root --password your_password\n"
"\n"
"# Specify tuning interval\n"
"auto-tune --db-type postgresql --interval 7200\n"
"\n"
"# Safe mode\n"
"auto-tune --db-type postgresql --safe-mode\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Best Practices\n"
"\n"
"1. **Backup First**: Back up the database before tuning\n"
"2. **Incremental Adjustment**: Adjust parameters gradually rather than all at once\n"
"3. **Monitor Effects**: Closely monitor database performance after tuning\n"
"4. **Regular Tuning**: Adjust parameters regularly based on workload changes\n"
"5. **Record Changes**: Record every parameter adjustment for rollback if needed\n"
"\n"
"## FAQ\n"
"\n"
"### Q: Will tuning affect database availability?\n"
"A: AutoTune uses safe mode by default, only adjusting parameters that do not require restarting the database. For parameters that require a restart, you will be prompted to confirm.\n"
"\n"
"### Q: How long does tuning take?\n"
"A: Tuning time depends on database size and workload complexity, typically ranging from a few minutes to tens of minutes.\n"
"\n"
"### Q: Can I manually specify parameters to tune?\n"
"A: Yes, you can specify the list of parameters to tune through the `parameters` parameter.\n"
"\n"
"### Q: What should I do if tuning results are not satisfactory?\n"
"A: You can use the `reset_config()` method to restore default configurations, or use `get_tuning_history()` to view historical records and manually select appropriate configurations.\n"
"\n"
"## License\n"
"\n"
"Apache 2.0 License\n"

